# 📝 Commit Template
#
# Use conventional commit format with semantic versioning patterns:
#
# 🚀 Major version bump (BREAKING CHANGE):
#   feat!: description (BREAKING CHANGE)
#   fix!: description (BREAKING CHANGE)
#
# 🎯 Minor version bump (new features/fixes):
#   feat: add new feature
#   fix: resolve issue
#   refactor: improve code
#
# 🐛 Patch version bump (default):
#   docs: update documentation
#   chore: maintenance tasks
#   test: add tests
#   style: formatting
#
# Examples:
#   feat: add automatic company matching system
#   fix: resolve database timeout issues
#   feat!: change API response format (BREAKING CHANGE)
#   refactor: improve rollout quota processing
#   docs: update setup guide
#
# The commit type determines version bump:
# - feat|fix|refactor → minor version (1.2.3 → 1.3.0)
# - ! suffix or BREAKING CHANGE → major version (1.2.3 → 2.0.0)
# - others → patch version (1.2.3 → 1.2.4)
